    },
    {
      "backgroundColor": "#fff3bf",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "text-00131",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "height": 610,
      "id": "rectangle-00130",
      "index": "b15",
      "roughness": 0,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 850671270,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1305288408,
      "width": 760,
      "x": 4706,
      "y": 330
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": "rectangle-00130",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 22,
      "height": 550,
      "id": "text-00131",
      "index": "b16",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "UX notes\n\n1. One door. The page never asks \"log in or sign up?\",\nthe question new users most often get wrong, so\nreturning and new educators follow the same path.\n\n2. Provider hint: a gmail.com, outlook.com or\nhotmail.com address suggests the matching single\nsign-on, which removes a password from the journey.\n\n3. Returning: the password field appears on the same\npage under the confirmed email, and Change goes back\nwithout losing anything.\n\n4. New: one confirmation, then straight into the Sign-up\narea (draft 2) with the email filled in.\n\nSingle sign-on buttons sit in one row below the email,\nso email stays the default and the providers stay one\nclick away.",
      "roughness": 0,
      "seed": 923345311,
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "text": "UX notes\n\n1. One door. The page never asks \"log in or sign up?\",\nthe question new users most often get wrong, so\nreturning and new educators follow the same path.\n\n2. Provider hint: a gmail.com, outlook.com or\nhotmail.com address suggests the matching single\nsign-on, which removes a password from the journey.\n\n3. Returning: the password field appears on the same\npage under the confirmed email, and Change goes back\nwithout losing anything.\n\n4. New: one confirmation, then straight into the Sign-up\narea (draft 2) with the email filled in.\n\nSingle sign-on buttons sit in one row below the email,\nso email stays the default and the providers stay one\nclick away.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
