      "x": 4706,
      "y": 2468
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": "rectangle-00331",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 22,
      "height": 1017.5,
      "id": "text-00332",
      "index": "b4L",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "UX notes\n\n1. Single sign-on gets one confirmation screen. What the\nsystem already knows (name and email from Google, role\nfrom the Join path) shows as a card to confirm, not as\nfields to fill.\n\n2. Date of birth is the one field left, and the hint\nsays why it's asked and that educators must be 18 or\nolder. The date is checked before the account is\ncreated.\n\n3. The Terms page and the policy checkbox are merged\ninto the submit button. All of the PDF's Sign-up fields\nare still collected, on one screen.\n\n4. Edit opens the name row in place, split into first\nand last name. Error state: an impossible date is called\nout with what to check.\n\n5. Email sign-ups use the same page with Name, Date of\nBirth and Password added. The live checklist stays (all\nrules met here). A Google link offers a way to skip the\npassword.\n\n6. Under 18, no account is created: the date field says\nwhy and the button stays off. Every educator is an\nadult, so there is no teen or under-13 path here. \"Join\nas a learner\" goes to the learner sign-up, with its own\nage rules. Back returns to the step before (this card,\nor the email form) with everything kept, so a mistyped\ndate can be fixed.\n\nRole shows as \"Joining as Educator\" with Change, not as\na field. If the educator didn't come through a teaching\npath, the row becomes a three-way choice: Learner,\nEducator, Parent or Guardian.",
      "roughness": 0,
      "seed": 1122708531,
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "text": "UX notes\n\n1. Single sign-on gets one confirmation screen. What the\nsystem already knows (name and email from Google, role\nfrom the Join path) shows as a card to confirm, not as\nfields to fill.\n\n2. Date of birth is the one field left, and the hint\nsays why it's asked and that educators must be 18 or\nolder. The date is checked before the account is\ncreated.\n\n3. The Terms page and the policy checkbox are merged\ninto the submit button. All of the PDF's Sign-up fields\nare still collected, on one screen.\n\n4. Edit opens the name row in place, split into first\nand last name. Error state: an impossible date is called\nout with what to check.\n\n5. Email sign-ups use the same page with Name, Date of\nBirth and Password added. The live checklist stays (all\nrules met here). A Google link offers a way to skip the\npassword.\n\n6. Under 18, no account is created: the date field says\nwhy and the button stays off. Every educator is an\nadult, so there is no teen or under-13 path here. \"Join\nas a learner\" goes to the learner sign-up, with its own\nage rules. Back returns to the step before (this card,\nor the email form) with everything kept, so a mistyped\ndate can be fixed.\n\nRole shows as \"Joining as Educator\" with Change, not as\na field. If the educator didn't come through a teaching\npath, the row becomes a three-way choice: Learner,\nEducator, Parent or Guardian.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1839118296,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 736,
      "x": 4718,
      "y": 2480
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 52,
      "height": 65,
      "id": "text-00333",
      "index": "b4M",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "Flow 3 · Create Team — Option 3: Auto Team",
      "roughness": 0,
