    {
      "backgroundColor": "#fff3bf",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "text-00564",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "height": 885,
      "id": "rectangle-00563",
      "index": "b84",
      "roughness": 0,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 301121357,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1849533096,
      "width": 760,
      "x": 6200,
      "y": 5517
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": "rectangle-00563",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 22,
      "height": 825,
      "id": "text-00564",
      "index": "b85",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "UX notes\n\n1. No Create Team step. After sign-up the system creates\n\"Maya Okafor's Team\" with her as owner. This follows the\nvault's Project 1 question: the Team exists to scope\n\"her cohorts\", and the vault itself suggests creating\nthat grouping automatically for an independent teacher.\nDraft 2 hands off straight to the Team Dashboard.\n\n2. A one-time banner explains in one line what the team\nis for and offers Rename. Nothing blocks the next step.\n\n3. Empty state: the first thing Maya decides is her\nclass (Create Cohort, draft 4), which is why she came.\n\n4. Rename happens inline on the dashboard. Error state:\nthe name is too long, with a one-click fix. With one\ncohort, the dashboard shows the table and the \"Cohort\nDashboard\" placeholder (solid here, dotted in the PDF).\n\n5. Open problem, answered \"later and elsewhere\": Invite\nTeam members leaves onboarding for Team Settings ›\nCo-Teachers. The page says learners are added inside\neach cohort, not here. Back and the breadcrumb return to\nthe Team Dashboard, sending nothing.\n\nRisk: learners and parents see \"Maya Okafor's Team\" if\nshe never renames it. That's acceptable for a solo\neducator and awkward for a co-op, so the banner stays\nuntil she renames it or dismisses it.",
      "roughness": 0,
      "seed": 1413055344,
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "text": "UX notes\n\n1. No Create Team step. After sign-up the system creates\n\"Maya Okafor's Team\" with her as owner. This follows the\nvault's Project 1 question: the Team exists to scope\n\"her cohorts\", and the vault itself suggests creating\nthat grouping automatically for an independent teacher.\nDraft 2 hands off straight to the Team Dashboard.\n\n2. A one-time banner explains in one line what the team\nis for and offers Rename. Nothing blocks the next step.\n\n3. Empty state: the first thing Maya decides is her\nclass (Create Cohort, draft 4), which is why she came.\n\n4. Rename happens inline on the dashboard. Error state:\nthe name is too long, with a one-click fix. With one\ncohort, the dashboard shows the table and the \"Cohort\nDashboard\" placeholder (solid here, dotted in the PDF).\n\n5. Open problem, answered \"later and elsewhere\": Invite\nTeam members leaves onboarding for Team Settings ›\nCo-Teachers. The page says learners are added inside\neach cohort, not here. Back and the breadcrumb return to\nthe Team Dashboard, sending nothing.\n\nRisk: learners and parents see \"Maya Okafor's Team\" if\nshe never renames it. That's acceptable for a solo\neducator and awkward for a co-op, so the banner stays\nuntil she renames it or dismisses it.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1474378712,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 736,
      "x": 6212,
      "y": 5529
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 52,
