    {
      "backgroundColor": "#fff3bf",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "text-00862",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "height": 967.5,
      "id": "rectangle-00861",
      "index": "bCs",
      "roughness": 0,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 37003358,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1874602408,
      "width": 760,
      "x": 4706,
      "y": 7719
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": "rectangle-00861",
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "fontSize": 22,
      "height": 907.5,
      "id": "text-00862",
      "index": "bCt",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "UX notes\n\n1. Arriving from a program link (draft 1, Option 4), the\nprogram is already selected and a banner says why.\nWithout a link, the same page shows a short program list\n(screen 2).\n\n2. The class name is suggested from the season, so a\nreturning educator can create a class with one click.\n\n3. A live side panel says what learners will get (open\nclass, workshops, how they join) and updates with the\nanswers.\n\n4. The NDPA question in plain words, No by default, with\na hint for homeschool groups, co-ops and clubs. Most\nType 8 educators never need to change it.\n\n5. Validation state: Create Class with nothing chosen\nshows both errors inline at once, no separate steps to\ngo back to.\n\n6. Yes (shown with a sample school teacher's class)\nexpands the explanation and a School name field in\nplace; the button becomes Send for Review.\n\n7. Pending review: learners can be added now and their\ninvites wait for approval, so the educator doesn't lose\nmomentum while Endless reviews.\n\nTrade-off: the page grows when Yes is chosen; the side\npanel has to stay short so the form stays above the\nfold.",
      "roughness": 0,
      "seed": 692530239,
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "text": "UX notes\n\n1. Arriving from a program link (draft 1, Option 4), the\nprogram is already selected and a banner says why.\nWithout a link, the same page shows a short program list\n(screen 2).\n\n2. The class name is suggested from the season, so a\nreturning educator can create a class with one click.\n\n3. A live side panel says what learners will get (open\nclass, workshops, how they join) and updates with the\nanswers.\n\n4. The NDPA question in plain words, No by default, with\na hint for homeschool groups, co-ops and clubs. Most\nType 8 educators never need to change it.\n\n5. Validation state: Create Class with nothing chosen\nshows both errors inline at once, no separate steps to\ngo back to.\n\n6. Yes (shown with a sample school teacher's class)\nexpands the explanation and a School name field in\nplace; the button becomes Send for Review.\n\n7. Pending review: learners can be added now and their\ninvites wait for approval, so the educator doesn't lose\nmomentum while Endless reviews.\n\nTrade-off: the page grows when Yes is chosen; the side\npanel has to stay short so the form stays above the\nfold.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 414360792,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 736,
      "x": 4718,
      "y": 7731
    },
    {
      "autoResize": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "containerId": null,
